{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"3e0ff0c3f6c757b9","name":"card_event_the_rock_of_gibraltar","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/OceaniaStorm/events/card_event_the_rock_of_gibraltar","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THE ROCK OF GIBRALTAR","text":"Develop a card in the enemy deck, then in your deck.","flavorText":"The Rock of Gibraltar held enormous strategic importance during WWII. Guarding the entrance to the Mediterranean, Gibraltar allowed Britain to protect vital shipping routes and maintain a strong naval and air presence close to North Africa and southern Europe. After war broke out in 1939, much of Gibraltar’s civilian population was evacuated so the territory could be transformed into a heavily fortified military base. By 1942, more than 30,000 British soldiers, sailors, and airmen were stationed on the Rock. Its existing network of tunnels was greatly expanded to provide protected accommodation, storage, communications, and defensive positions deep inside the limestone. Britain even prepared for the possibility of Gibraltar being captured. Under the secret Operation codenamed Tracer, a small team was ready to be sealed inside hidden tunnels to observe and report enemy movements. The plan was never needed, and Gibraltar remained firmly in British hands throughout the war.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.develop"],"Name":"card_event_the_rock_of_gibraltar","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_the_rock_of_gibraltar_title","SourceString":"THE ROCK OF GIBRALTAR","LocalizedString":"THE ROCK OF GIBRALTAR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_the_rock_of_gibraltar_text","SourceString":"Develop a card in the enemy deck, then in your deck.","LocalizedString":"Develop a card in the enemy deck, then 